{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod","id":806355,"title":"Anyone else dislike how Asia is handled in WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-11T12:54:11-08:00","id":806355,"title":"Anyone else dislike how Asia is handled in WoD","content":"Out of curiosity, does anyone else have a problem with how White Wolf handled Asia. I personally like the kuei-jin, but in my opinion all the other supplements are horrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:07:08-08:00","id":806375,"title":"","content":"MANY People have gone on tangents about the issue... sadly most often ON the kuei-jin bashing them as &quot;Orientalist mary sues&quot; <br /> <br /> I didnt find it PERFECT Mind you The hengoayoki beast courts, while an obstacle to garou nation packs... negotiating with the courts to get permission to work in a area, can be a fun obstacle I think...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:46:41-08:00","id":806434,"title":"","content":"The land of kung fu and anime, consisting entirely of China, Japan, and India?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm not a huge fan. Fingers crossed for the 20th Anniversary Editions to have a more refined touch when it comes to everywhere that isn't America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:51:25-08:00","id":806441,"title":"","content":"KOTE has issues I personally like that there's other types of vampires out there vs Kindred all the time for there to be contrast, it plays up premises vastly differently on the other hand well I'm sure plenty of people will give you those flaws.<br /> <br /> The Hengeyokai are what a large subportion of the W:TA really want &quot;We can play all our Fera together&quot; fortunately the new Fera book gave some other options for people who don't want to be as caught up in Asian cultures.<br /> <br /> Dark Kingdom of Jade pretty much makes sense with Wraith's premises so I'm ok with that.<br /> <br /> Hsien I want to like conceptually but the magic could use more explanation and they don't really have any interactions with the Dreaming at all. Plus Tanuki are real animals.<br /> <br /> Mage: why does no one ever bring up the Super secret better than the Technocracy Asian Technocracy that is slightly more mystical because asians are clearly more respectful of mysticism, who have so totally fooled the Technocracy that they can do whatever they want. I really hope Technocracy Reloaded Fixes the &quot;Five Elemental Dragons&quot; especially since the Technocracy is supposed to be a metaphor for Colonialism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:32:50-08:00","id":806475,"title":"","content":"Yeah... I think most fans consider the WoD's handling of Asia problematic at best. While the books run a rather large spectrum in terms of quality in this regard, it is kind of a generally accepted consensus of the fandom that any book primarily set in Asia in the original WoD books is going to at least have something cringe worthy in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:45:59-08:00","id":806484,"title":"","content":"Dark Kingdom of Jade seems to be the rare exception, though it still largely views Asia as &quot;outdated China plus Japan&quot; rather than as a massive continent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:02:27-08:00","id":806494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=806475#post806475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... I think most fans consider the WoD's handling of Asia problematic at best. While the books run a rather large spectrum in terms of quality in this regard, it is kind of a generally accepted consensus of the fandom that any book primarily set in original WoD books is going to at least have something cringe worthy in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There Fixed it, The idea that Asia was particularly cringe worthy is what I take issue with. I find Asia to be par for the course for CWoD in 1998. And while KOTE will always have some Orientalism.. so too will the rest of cwod will be built on cultural fetishism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:06:57-08:00","id":806497,"title":"","content":"Actually, I wish the rest of the setting more resembled Asia, with more interaction, some of it nonviolent between the various splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:25:21-08:00","id":806516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=806441#post806441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KOTE has issues I personally like that there's other types of vampires out there vs Kindred all the time for there to be contrast...</div> </div> </div> </div>It annoyed me that the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">kuei-jin aren't really vampires and have more to do with WRAITH than VAMPIRE as they are pretty much just a Special, Asian Soul only, type of Risen. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:45:58-08:00","id":806612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=806516#post806516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It annoyed me that the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">kuei-jin aren't really vampires and have more to do with WRAITH than VAMPIRE as they are pretty much just a Special, Asian Soul only, type of Risen. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's less about special Asian Souls and more about which set of spirits has claims to your soul. The Yama Kings are essentially perverting the normal way things work in Asia, and that's why we have the Thousand Hells and a way for the Kuei Jin to come back as they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:49:16-08:00","id":806613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=806516#post806516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It annoyed me that the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">kuei-jin aren't really vampires and have more to do with WRAITH than VAMPIRE as they are pretty much just a Special, Asian Soul only, type of Risen. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>They go through a lot of stages that resemble other critters - starting as something like a zombie or hungry ghost, they progress toward vampirism, then as more direct life force stealers. It would be more accurate to say that they aren't always vampires, but they certainly do qualify at most Dharma levels that you'd be likely to play. Also, they're distinct from Risen in that, unlike normal ghosts, they've been broken apart and put back together again; normal ghosts never suffer the severing of psyche and shadow at the moment of death. Now if we could just have that principle apply outside of KotE...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T18:01:41-08:00","id":806626,"title":"","content":"I have yet to read a White Wolf book that does not contain something genuinely cringe-worthy. The quality of ideas presented could vary dramatically within a work to say the least. I really don't know how it's possible to soberly run most of these gamelines without substantial personal/group edits to various backstory and setting elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T18:18:12-08:00","id":806634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=806494#post806494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There I demonstrated that I care more about being a pedantic asshat than productive conversation by editing your post</div> </div> </div> </div>There, I said what you didn't have the balls to say. You might notice... it doesn't fix things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea that Asia was particularly cringe worthy is what I take issue with. </div> </div> </div>Tha'ts nice. That's not my opinion, which is that Asia was handled in a particularly cringe worthy way (which you seem to have trouble recognizing people can think and still acknowledge all the other cringe worthy stuff in the WOD). Asia in the WoD (which is not just the Year of the Lotus), got it worse than average for the WoD. I'll go way farther back to things like Do and Kailindo where Asians have a monopoly on supernatural martial arts, katanas having better stats than other one-handed swords, and the Wu Keng Craft. Yeah I don't need to just harp on KotE or even the YotL.<br /> <br /> The thread also wasn't &quot;WoD presentation of Asia in 1998,&quot; but as a whole. Which means the Orientalism that was baked into the games from the get go is plenty relevant. So for a second thread, that's remind you that I don't need to go in with all my problems with the WoD's treatment of Native American peoples to express my opinions about how it dealt with Asian people (and not just people, which is part of the problem).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:43:30-08:00","id":806723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=806634#post806634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">katanas having better stats than other one-handed swords.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see a problem with this. Should I?<br /> <br /> Though, to be honest, I don't see a problem with a lot of the stuff in older WW books because:<br /> <br /> a) it either doesn't affect me<br /> b) It's targeting people like me(like the &quot;Irish werewolves being drunk, etc.&quot; in which I'm Irish and don't have a problem with this at all. And I LOVE to drink and I don't really care about crap like this. I drink. My family drinks. If I turned into a 10 foot tall werewolf, I would probably continue to drink. <br /> <br /> or <br /> <br /> c) Sometimes, I think people are looking for things that aren't there. I do understand there is definitely some material that some people might be offended by--especially if it's people that are directly offended by the material. If so, update it so the material is less offensive. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But I'm not also not for changing every single stereotype that can be found in mass media and entertainment.</span></span></span>And, well, like I've said before; I think Onyx Path has handled the <i>new</i> books with utmost respect(Assamites, Ravnos, etc.) and I have little fear that this won't continue. Even with their depictions of Asia. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:39:56-08:00","id":806759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=806723#post806723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't see a problem with this. Should I?<br /> <br /> Though, to be honest, I don't see a problem with a lot of the stuff in older WW books because:<br /> <br /> a) it either doesn't affect me</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop. Consider this. Dwell on it for some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:59:18-08:00","id":806772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=806516#post806516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It annoyed me that the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">kuei-jin aren't really vampires and have more to do with WRAITH than VAMPIRE as they are pretty much just a Special, Asian Soul only, type of Risen. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing I like about KOTE is that it is better about following Asian ideas of a vampire rather than just slapping western vampires in an oriental setting. I personally wish they did a similar thing for Africa. <br /> <br /> I took issue with the werewolf stuff which is also a complaint I have with werewolf in general is they will take some mythological creature's name and just slap it onto something. Tengu personally annoys me and fomori should be a type of Fae.<br /> <br /> Mage also was annoying is that they didn't use the many real world magical beliefs that did and in cases still do exist in Asia and instead used a bunch stereotypes that had a little bit of research on them.<br /> <br /> Can't say much for wraith as I haven't read it's Asia supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","user":"stanlemon","date":". 01-12-2016, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:59:59-08:00","id":806773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=806723#post806723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't see a problem with this. Should I?</div> </div> </div> </div>On top of Saur Ops Specialists far more important point:<br /> <br /> Katanas aren't better swords by virtue of some sort of exceptional design. Either the game should keep all weapons in a fairly simulation oriented abstraction where &quot;this is a cool weapon!' doesn't give it stat bonuses, or the Rule of Cool should be the default and weapon stats should be based on how cool they are. and screw reality.<br /> <br /> Having weapons that mostly mirror reality, except a few weapons that stand out as having far better stats than makes sense compared to similar weapons because it's cool (esp. when the game is not built around this sort of mentality), is a design problem.<br /> <br /> When what gets considered cool is part of a larger pattern... well see posts above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T07:12:44-08:00","id":806986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=806759#post806759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stop. Consider this. Dwell on it for some time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I did. For a few minutes. Sorry. I never claimed to be the most sympathetic of individuals, and like I said before, I'm simply not easily offended when it comes to stuff like this. But in no way am I telling people what they should or should be offended by. If something offends you or bothers you, by all means...<br /> <br /> I gave the example of the Fianna being the drunk Irish werewolves. I meant it. I couldn't care less. Doesn't bother me.<br /> <br /> I'm just NOT one of those people. *shrugs*<br /> <br /> Anyways, I'm definitely for Asia(or any continent for that matter) being handled with respect for any and all cultures and ethnic groups involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 01-12-2016, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T09:32:36-08:00","id":807082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=806986#post806986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry. I never claimed to be the most sympathetic of individuals, and like I said before, I'm simply not easily offended when it comes to stuff like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to be.<br /> <br /> The point though, only caring about what directly affects us is actually a pretty shitty way to avoid not telling people what they should be offended by, and an extremely shitty way to get to books that handle the material in a better fashion. &quot;I don't care if it doesn't affect me, and I have a thick skin about stuff that does,&quot; is pretty much the foundational psychology of institutionalized discrimination.<br /> <br /> Just going on self-interest: If the books perpetuate things that other people find distasteful, it reduces the number of people that want to play the games, and the number of people that buy the games. If those numbers drop too low, you run out of people to play with, and you stop getting new awesome books.<br /> <br /> You don't have to be sympathetic, or empathetic. Just be selfish in your desire to have more, and better, WoD books, which is only accomplished by having more people get into the games, which requires making the games appealing to more people. This means listening to complaints about the content seriously, and instead of tossing up the, &quot;why should I care?&quot; flag, either just acknowledge the problem, or actually consider how to fix it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T15:53:04-08:00","id":807373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807082#post807082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just be selfish in your desire to have more, and better, WoD books, which is only accomplished by having more people get into the games, which requires making the games appealing to more people. This means listening to complaints about the content seriously, and instead of tossing up the, &quot;why should I care?&quot; flag, <b>either just acknowledge the problem, or actually consider how to fix it.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the problem. I've never had issues playing some of the parts of the WoD people have had trouble playing. Assamites, Ravnos, etc. I don't find issues with them. This is a game, that's supposed to be reflective of our world, but...much darker. All the stereotypes that EXIST in the real world, all the shit, the crime, the negativity, the drugs, sex, etc. that is in the real world, can be found in the World of Darkness. That has always appealed to me. The world is a shitty place. It doesn't bother me that the Assamites are a clan of assassins from the Middle East, for the same reason it didn't bother me one of the signature characters from VtM can only feed from rape victims. And why I think having Slashers as playable characters in Hunter 2 is an excellent idea.<br /> There are much &quot;lighter&quot; games I can play. But as a horror fan, the WoD--warts and all, is something that has always appealed to me. Someone is always going to find something to be offended by, regardless of their location, regardless of their ideologies. <br /> <br /> I just want to play the games, man. <br /> <br /> And another issue? As per my example, I <b>don't</b> consider the Fianna a problem. So there's nothing to acknowledge. I don't see a need to &quot;fix&quot; it. It's not broken, to me. Of course, that's just one example. I guess the katana would be another.<br /> <br /> There are a number of other examples where I probably WOULD see a problem. And if it's fixed? Cool. Otherwise...<br /> <br /> It's clear we're not going to see eye to eye on this, and that's perfectly fine. Keep on gaming!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T17:58:39-08:00","id":807472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807373#post807373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's the problem. I've never had issues playing some of the parts of the WoD people have had trouble <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But other people have, often when they <u>are</u> affected. Besides, these things are often the results of research failures, so there's that, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T18:45:50-08:00","id":807497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807373#post807373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's the problem. I've never had issues playing some of the parts of the WoD people have had trouble playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter if you personally haven't had a problem with things. It matters that you acknowledge that other people have problems with the same things. A white man doesn't need to suffer the racism of the US criminal justice system personally to acknowledge it exists, or say, &quot;This doesn't directly impact me, but I can see why it should change.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All the stereotypes that EXIST in the real world,... </div> </div> </div>There is a huge difference between playing in a game world where discriminatory stereotypes are reflective of the ones in our world, and one that makes discriminatory stereotypes <i>metaphysically true.</i><br /> <br /> That's the line that really gets to people. Are drunken Irish werewolves a thing? Sure. So are drunken Irish humans. The thing is that the Fianna aren't actually just drunken Irish werewolves, and they're not forced to be so by fluff or by mechanics. There's no trait in the game that says, &quot;You're either Irish, or of Irish decent. You have to spend WP to resist getting drunk whenever you have the chance, and you lose 2 dice on social rolls if you don't talk in a strong accent or in Irish Gaelic. All ethnically Irish PCs must take this to be considered truly Irish.&quot;<br /> <br /> The game doesn't go off the rails just because characters happen to intersect with real world stereotypes in various ways. The games become problems when they force stereotypes on characters.<br /> <br /> That's the difference between the Assamites, and a signature Ventrue who's feeding restriction is triggery. You don't have to play a Venture that only feeds on rape victims. Such a Ventrue never has to be in any of your games just because the books have one in them. You can't use the Assamites without bringing in game-enforced anti-Arab/Muslim/Middle-Eastern stereotypes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Someone is always going to find something to be offended by, regardless of their location, regardless of their ideologies. </div> </div> </div>Cop out response. The correct response to this is not, &quot;so screw caring about judging the situations, and just be careless about how offensive you are.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is not a black &amp; white, yes or no, issue. We are capable of looking at a complaint about something in the games, recognize why people had a bad experience because of the game's writing, and then making rational judgements on (1) if the complaint is something truly wrong with the game, or the game and the individual being a bad fit - plenty of people just aren't going to enjoy the subjects the WoD touches on - (2) if the issue at hand can be fixed for future use by addressing the problems and rectifying them with better text, or (3) if the issue really is something that can only be fixed by excising the material and starting over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just want to play the games, man. </div> </div> </div>What makes you think the rest of us don't?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And another issue? As per my example, I <b>don't</b> consider the Fianna a problem. So there's nothing to acknowledge. I don't see a need to &quot;fix&quot; it. It's not broken, to me. Of course, that's just one example. I guess the katana would be another. </div> </div> </div>What's to acknowledge is when people make valid complaints about the Fianna as presented in the books. Or valid complaints about katana stats.<br /> <br /> All you're doing is saying, &quot;My opinion is all that matters, so if someone presents a reason why my opinion might need to be reanalyzed, I have to attack such positions to preserve the primacy of my opinions.&quot;<br /> <br /> You come off as caring far more about the purity of your idealized concept of the games, and shouting down changes (even if you'll acknowledge they might be positive overall changes), than actually having people game on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:49:01-08:00","id":807535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no trait in the game that says, &quot;You're either Irish, or of Irish decent. You have to spend WP to resist getting drunk whenever you have the chance, and you lose 2 dice on social rolls if you don't talk in a strong accent or in Irish Gaelic. All ethnically Irish PCs must take this to be considered truly Irish. </div> </div> </div>It's already been pointed out in this thread that WW can't always manage to accurately depict a culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:56:17-08:00","id":807540,"title":"","content":"My problem is less them not getting things accurate and more them perverting it. Werewolf is especially bad at this but all the games have the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T20:03:35-08:00","id":807543,"title":"","content":"The original corebooks did a good job at describing the general society of a worldwide supernatural group. We could assume there were local differences, but the Camarilla was a worldwide organization, the Litany was the prehistoric law of the Garou, the Traditions were an alliance that incorporated all magical traditions, and ghosts were dead no matter what (although the various depictions of mythological underworlds were explained). I really liked that.<br /> <br /> Then, as the game developed, people kept shrinking what these groups were and said they only applied to the West. Everyone else was their own thing, and often had completely different game mechanics. They took the late twentieth century concept of muliculturalism and retroactively applied it back even though it made no sense. White Wolf thought they were doing justice to other cultures when it was just the opposite. It made the game less cool. As bad as Asia was, Africa was equally so.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with there being some mysteries in the game, and saying a chronicle set in Asia would be different than in the West (well, duh) is fine. But it was just became overboard. Given the long timeline vampire, I never understood why the Kuei-jin were so unknown in early editions, but it was so minor it could be easily ignored - and wasn't any worse than any of the other bloodlines. Then it all became cheesey nonsense.<br /> <br /> In my own games, I ignore most of these later supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T20:07:28-08:00","id":807544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807497#post807497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You come off as caring far more about the purity of your idealized concept of the games, and shouting down changes (even if you'll acknowledge they might be positive overall changes), than actually having people game on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. I just disagree with you. On many things regarding what should and/or shouldn't be changed. That's it. No one's &quot;shouting.&quot; No one thinks their opinion is more holier than the other. I simply don't agree. Which, is perfectly fine. <br /> <br /> Seeing a lot of words being put into my mouth though, and I honestly lack the energy to keep this up. So I'll take my &quot;cop out&quot; responses and check out of the thread. Enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T02:07:39-08:00","id":807722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807543#post807543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original corebooks did a good job at describing the general society of a worldwide supernatural group. We could assume there were local differences, but the Camarilla was a worldwide organization, the Litany was the prehistoric law of the Garou, the Traditions were an alliance that incorporated all magical traditions, and ghosts were dead no matter what (although the various depictions of mythological underworlds were explained). I really liked that..</div> </div> </div> </div>NO they didn't. The Camarilla and Sabbat are very American with some work plays out in Europe, its built on the back of American views of pop christanity. The Majority of Tribes in Werewolf have a strong basis in European stereotypes and amazingly here's another thing... Wolves don't live everywhere. The Traditions are just as bad for majority western take.. and are explicitly hit at in setting for being so while claiming universality. Ghosts had different powers depending on where they were from and some had completely different setups. There was never a universal world of Darkness even the earliest books had it as a patchwork of conflicting realms and mythologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T02:24:22-08:00","id":807729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807543#post807543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my own games, I ignore most of these later supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an odd statement considering that some of the worst and most offensive material stems from the first edition. Originaly all the Eastern Vampires were Gaki and Bushi (yup, they were all Japanese, I always thought that the name Kuei Jin was actually a desperate attempt to be inclusive after that) who hated the Western Vampires and who were implied to be &quot;different&quot; from the Children of Caine. That was so well thought out and researched. The original Ravnos were almost as bad as WoD Gypsies. Assamites were little better. Dreamspeakers? Oh Boy. Now that's a whole world of pain.<br /> <br /> ... I mean, where does one even stop? &quot;Inappropriate&quot; is a very good word for the early WOD. Later books really made an effort to make things better. They didn't always succeeed, but at least they made an effort.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T04:33:55-08:00","id":807775,"title":"","content":"Yup, in my games, East Asia is dominated by Cainites. There's no place for the Kuei-Jin at my gaming table. I like having East Asia accessible to vampires, thank you very much.<br /> <br /> That being said, while regular vampires control East Asia in my games, the Camarilla and Sabbat do not as those two organizations are uniquely a Western thing, having stemmed from the aftermath of the Inquisition. Instead, the cities of Asia are controlled by indigenous vampire courts (similar to the Kuei-Jin courts but with vampires instead) and they see no need for the Camarilla and Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Rule Zero is a wonderful thing, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T04:49:42-08:00","id":807781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807775#post807775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, in my games, East Asia is dominated by Cainites. There's no place for the Kuei-Jin at my gaming table. I like having East Asia accessible to vampires, thank you very much.<br /> <br /> That being said, while regular vampires control East Asia in my games, the Camarilla and Sabbat do not as those two organizations are uniquely a Western thing, having stemmed from the aftermath of the Inquisition. Instead, the cities of Asia are controlled by indigenous vampire courts (similar to the Kuei-Jin courts but with vampires instead) and they see no need for the Camarilla and Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Rule Zero is a wonderful thing, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I've played games where KOTE style vampires were the universal vampire type with Kindred being nonexistant, things ended up fitting much better with Wraith, Mage, Werewolf, Changeling that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T05:19:29-08:00","id":807794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807775#post807775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, in my games, East Asia is dominated by Cainites. There's no place for the Kuei-Jin at my gaming table. I like having East Asia accessible to vampires, thank you very much.<br /> <br /> That being said, while regular vampires control East Asia in my games, the Camarilla and Sabbat do not as those two organizations are uniquely a Western thing, having stemmed from the aftermath of the Inquisition. Instead, the cities of Asia are controlled by indigenous vampire courts (similar to the Kuei-Jin courts but with vampires instead) and they see no need for the Camarilla and Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Rule Zero is a wonderful thing, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you even bother reading what I wrote? The original Gaki and Bushi were pretty much Kill Whitey and &quot;why don't they act like Cainites&quot; even back in First Edition. And the point was that the First Editons were a horrifying mess of preconceptions, stereotypes, racism and utter cluelessnes about the world beyond America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T05:28:01-08:00","id":807795,"title":"","content":"I wish Vampire hadn't been so dead set on the Curse of Caine and Christian mythology as the origination story. This made it difficult to impossible to include vampires from other societies with different origins that might not be based off of Christian mythology.<br /> <br /> While there were issues with Kindred of the East, I have to give it credit for creating a different type of Vampire, rather than simply trying to shoehorn other cultures blood suckling demons into the Christian Vampire mythos like Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom did.<br /> <br /> The implications in that book, that the native African's beliefs were wrong and the European Vampire's beliefs about Caine were correct, along with plenty of winks and nods towards existing Vampire factions, were very unfortunate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-13-2016, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T06:21:56-08:00","id":807820,"title":"","content":"Sadly so, Anubis.<br /> <br /> It would have been an amazing twist if the Laibon were actually right, but I am assuming that most Vampire fans would have found themselves cheated out of all the hubub built around the antedelluvians and Caine. Which is kinda absurd since the majority of the games never really were about the actual origin of vampirism nor was it especailly relevant to Vampire as a game.<br /> <br /> I think the one thing Requiem did really well was that it made the Wicked Dead book. Lately I've been looking at vampires through a Night's Black Agents lens, and I really appreciate the toolbox and openended mythology inherit in that system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8760,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","user":"Cogliostro","date":". 01-13-2016, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T07:25:40-08:00","id":807863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807820#post807820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly so, Anubis.<br /> <br /> It would have been an amazing twist if the Laibon were actually right, but I am assuming that most Vampire fans would have found themselves cheated out of all the hubub built around the antedelluvians and Caine. Which is kinda absurd since the majority of the games never really were about the actual origin of vampirism nor was it especailly relevant to Vampire as a game.<br /> <br /> I think the one thing Requiem did really well was that it made the Wicked Dead book. Lately I've been looking at vampires through a Night's Black Agents lens, and I really appreciate the toolbox and openended mythology inherit in that system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I prefer that the Real Truth be ambiguous - and so it is in my game. Now, we have in cannon that ravnos's death-frenzy took down a group of KoTEK, even as it did the Ravnos themselves.. which suggests that the thing that died in India founded both. It in no way proves that the thing that died in india is 1.) A child of Caine, 2.) Traces its lineage purely to Mesopotamia, or 3.) Identified strictly with the Ravnos.<br /> <br /> While I -like- many lines going back to Mesopotamia (Sumerians are cool, yo!), I like ambiguity at the beginning, rather than certainty. As I've said other places, if you must have Caine, but are uncomfortable with 'all truth comes from Judaism', then just make 'Caine' a mantle of a story hung over the shoulders of the first-cursed man (early sin and curses not being specific to Judaism!) by the medieval, christian vampires of Europe. Ill admit, I always found it a bit strange to have pre-Sumerian beings described by a purely Babylonian or later set of stories...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9449-marcus-smythe","name":"Marcus Smythe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T08:18:00-08:00","id":807899,"title":"","content":"I think the prevalence of discussions such as these shows why it needs fixing. But I'm still not sure how, exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T08:33:11-08:00","id":807915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807794#post807794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original Gaki and Bushi were pretty much Kill Whitey and &quot;why don't they act like Cainites&quot; even back in First Edition. And the point was that the First Editons were a horrifying mess of preconceptions, stereotypes, racism and utter cluelessnes about the world beyond America.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you're using the term first edition correctly. The Bushi, for example, are already second edition material -- the 2nd ed corebook came out in 1992 and <i>Dark Alliance: Vancouver</i> was published in 1993.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the original writeups of the Independent clans in the first edition <i>Players Guide</i> are, as a general thing, <i>less</i> cringeworthy than the various second edition clanbooks. The Ravnos, for example, were not originally conceived as &quot;gypsy vampires&quot; -- while the writeup mentions that Ravnos had latched onto the cultures of various traveling peoples (the Rom among them), they tended to get <i>rejected</i> by the people more often than not. The original Ravnos weakness was not compulsive lying and theft, but an eldritch aura of unease -- <i>much like the nWoD Nosferatu weakness.</i> What's more, the initial Ravnos writeup implied that some of the injustices done to Romani people throughout history happened because <i>they were exploited by the Ravnos parasites among them.</i><br /> <br /> Similarly, the Giovanni were originally <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/610856-changes-new-thing-we-want-to-see-in-the-new-edition?p=612440#post612440\">the modern Borgias</a>, not &quot;Italian mafia vampires.&quot; Their writeup doesn't even mention the mob -- that's material from the second edition Giovanni clanbook. The Assamites and Followers of Set were described as originally hailing from a specific culture, but having long since diversified into something else than just the &quot;Arab clan&quot; and the &quot;Egyptian clan.&quot; It's curious how all of the Independents became <i>more</i> stereotypical and sometimes outright racist during the second edition run, leaving the revised edition to clean up the mess made during the previous iteration of the rules, rather than what was originally presented in the first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 01-13-2016, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T08:43:19-08:00","id":807923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807820#post807820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would have been an amazing twist if the Laibon were actually right, but I am assuming that most Vampire fans would have found themselves cheated out of all the hubub built around the antedelluvians and Caine. Which is kinda absurd since the majority of the games never really were about the actual origin of vampirism nor was it especailly relevant to Vampire as a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Caine and the Antediluvians don't matter one whit in the vast majority of chronicles that people run. I've always liked the idea that many of the Laibon legacies represent far older strains of vampirism than the modern Western clans -- the Guruhi as the ancestors of the Nosferatu, for example -- regardless of what the books may or may not imply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T08:52:29-08:00","id":807927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807915#post807915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you're using the term first edition correctly. The Bushi, for example, are already second edition material -- the 2nd ed corebook came out in 1992 and <i>Dark Alliance: Vancouver</i> was published in 1993.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the original writeups of the Independent clans in the first edition <i>Players Guide</i> are, as a general thing, <i>less</i> cringeworthy than the various second edition clanbooks. The Ravnos, for example, were not originally conceived as &quot;gypsy vampires&quot; -- while the writeup mentions that Ravnos had latched onto the cultures of various traveling peoples (the Rom among them), they tended to get <i>rejected</i> by the people more often than not. The original Ravnos weakness was not compulsive lying and theft, but an eldritch aura of unease -- <i>much like the nWoD Nosferatu weakness.</i> What's more, the initial Ravnos writeup implied that some of the injustices done to Romani people throughout history happened because <i>they were exploited by the Ravnos parasites among them.</i><br /> <br /> Similarly, the Giovanni were originally <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/610856-changes-new-thing-we-want-to-see-in-the-new-edition?p=612440#post612440\">the modern Borgias</a>, not &quot;Italian mafia vampires.&quot; Their writeup doesn't even mention the mob -- that's material from the second edition Giovanni clanbook. The Assamites and Followers of Set were described as originally hailing from a specific culture, but having long since diversified into something else than just the &quot;Arab clan&quot; and the &quot;Egyptian clan.&quot; It's curious how all of the Independents became <i>more</i> stereotypical and sometimes outright racist during the second edition run, leaving the revised edition to clean up the mess made during the previous iteration of the rules, rather than what was originally presented in the first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I actually assumed the original clanbooks were first edition, considering that in Mage and Werewolf things started improving the futher we got away from First Edition. Of course, we still had lovely thinks like the Black Furies book or the Children of Gaia book in Revised :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T08:53:43-08:00","id":807928,"title":"","content":"Requiem (mostly during the late 1st edition and 2nd edition) got a lot of things right, and I wouldn't feel the need to occasionally jump ship to Masquerade for some chronicles, if Requiem paid more attention to fleshing out a concrete toolbox setting. The Wicked Dead book, for example, was great and useful, but it feels like a D&amp;D Monster Manual, that doesn't do the fourth wall any favors... They were a minor template without a powerstat, and there was no organization or culture inherent to these creatures. For some reason, a lot of nwod creatures are comfortable with voluntary isolation for no apparent reason whatsoever...<br /> <br /> The corebook and the Secrets of the Covenants slightly departed from the city crawler recipe, by mentioning the Sons of Phobos outside their respective book (Blood Sorcery) in the Jiang Shi write-up. Still, that game needs more of what Masquerade has <i>too much of</i>, namely some basic continuity (don't need 4 slightly different versions of the Strix across the books, but would love some fluff that plays down the birdie aspect and more the vampiric demon aspect and how they plot to bring down Kindred society for example) and more of the Requiem clanbook love in the form of concrete NPCs who do more than just try to hold some petty, seasonal title in their respective domains and nothing more. King of the playground doesn't mean much to adults after all...<br /> <br /> Anyway, enough of me derailing the thread. From my (scarce) WoD 1st ed experience, the books got the formula right. I agree with Elphilm, second edition often went gonzo stereotypical for no good reason, while some of Revised (and early Requiem) felt like it hated itself.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of non-Kindred eastern Vampires, but doing such a concept justice would mean digging deeper than the cultural surface, into philosophical, theological, and metaphysical differences between said cultures. How can you possibly teach damnation to a person who does not believe in sin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 01-13-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T14:09:04-08:00","id":808219,"title":"","content":"A question - given the level of scholarship that lies behind having a clan of philosopher warriors named for... witches, I think... a clan of artists named for bull-fighters... all the other errors and liberties taken with the western world in the books written about western vampires... Is it possible to write a game set in other cultures that would not anger people? What level of scholarship and research do we expect of people who are, ultimately, writing pretendy-fun-time game books set in a world similar, but not identical to our own? What are some games/game supplements set in eastern culture that are not problematic, and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9449-marcus-smythe","name":"Marcus Smythe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T15:36:47-08:00","id":808284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus Smythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=808219#post808219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to write a game set in other cultures that would not anger people?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Look at the CofD. One of the advantages of the clean slate it had, was to head off this sort of thing from the beginning. Which isn't to say that the CofD never angers people, or is batting 100% on this, but the culturally problematic stuff is by far an exception. Not all if this is research (though that helps). A lot of it is not linking general character groups to specific real world cultures in the first place; instead the rules allow for specific adjustable and/or optional groups that can be used for modifying the game to a local culture. When the authors want to right settings for other cultures, they have all the tools they need to do so in the extant material. It is designed to be adapted to locations (and even eras) of choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What level of scholarship and research do we expect of people who are, ultimately, writing pretendy-fun-time game books set in a world similar, but not identical to our own? </div> </div> </div>Enough to treat the material with respect. Nobody's actually looking for perfection, but enough knowledge about the subject matter to actually portray a world similar but not identical to our own, instead of a world populated by misinformed stereotypes from our own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:01:18-08:00","id":808320,"title":"","content":"I wrote a really long post, so I thought I'd summarize instead.<br /> <br /> There is a fine line between realism and racism, sensitivity and bland back story.<br /> <br /> It's been difficult for both worlds to strike perfection, so I don't suggest going into either extremes.<br /> <br /> RPGs need realism and stirring critical thought in the minds of players to compete with modern forms of entertainment, IMHO. So I like my NPCs racist or prejudiced, but clans, sects, etc. require a well-based understanding of the cultures and philosophies they are dealing with.<br /> <br /> The solution is not removing Malkavians, it's studying psychology, psychiatry, watching how mental illness really works, and at the same time how in the past some sufferers managed to be regarded as geniuses or oracles.<br /> <br /> Bottom line: The world is shit, the world of darkness is shittier. As long as writers understand what they're writing about in detail (and can become passionate about it), I don't think certain topics should be off limits.<br /> <br /> The Giovani may have been intended as modern Borgias, but according to Wikipedia, the Borgias operated much like mobsters of their time. So in the 60s through 90s, it's likely that the clan focused on mob business. I suggest watching I cento passi, to see how much the mafia had infiltrated everyday life even in rural Italy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 01-13-2016, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:43:25-08:00","id":808337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807722#post807722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NO they didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note I said original corebooks and not First Edition material. Things were only described in a very sketchy way in the corebooks since page count was limited, and it is infodumping a lot. Since it was an American company producing things for a predominantly American market, of course it's going to present things from an American perspective. But precisely because it was kept vague, one could work out much details on their own if they wanted to set a game elsewhere.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla and Sabbat were presented as worldwide organizations. They were not limited to only the West. In the very early sourcebooks, you ever had examples that their members were worldwide to support that. Chicago Primogen were dominated by a Muslim Nosferatu and African Gangrel despite being a very American city. Werewolf had some prominent Tribes based on European lore, but Native American Tribes were also predominant, and the descriptions of other Tribes tied them into the Middle East, Asia, and India. For those areas without wolves, they brought in other shapechangers more appropriate for those lands. Mage presented its Traditions in very large archetypes. Some were more Western in orientation, while others were more Eastern or other. Several Traditions were obviously much more heavily based on non-Western ideas and culture.<br /> <br /> As these things were developed, it got worse - mainly because a bonehead mistake or ideas early on had to be perpetuated throughout the game line because of &quot;canon.&quot; Or that the authors wrote what they knew about or thought cool, so they ignored a lot of things that could have been included. So if you want to complain about how some/many of the supplements were bad or bad in certain aspects, I will join you. However, I still feel the original corebooks (1st and 2nd edition) were mainly good, and their ideas could be applied practically anywhere.<br /> <br /> As the game line developed, WW started backing away from the idea that the societies introduced int he corebooks were worldwide. So instead of Asia including Camarilla vampires, even India became dominant by one Clan, and mostly excluded from all of East Asia. The Garou of China seemed to have all become Stargazers and were involved in a very different set up (the Beast Courts) than the rest of the Garou Nation. Dead people's souls in Asia and Africa were explicitly different and reflected in game mechanics, instead of just adhering/beloning to some different Lord of the Dead.<br /> <br /> Later editions were explicitly different than how I imagined things when the original corebooks first came out, and their development was not intrinsic to the original set up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:48:39-08:00","id":808342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807795#post807795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish Vampire hadn't been so dead set on the Curse of Caine and Christian mythology as the origination story. This made it difficult to impossible to include vampires from other societies with different origins that might not be based off of Christian mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never saw this as a problem. Attributing the origin to Cain was something the Abrahamic religions would naturally do. I never thought that vampires embraced prior to the rise of Christianity or Islam would attribute their origin to some obscure Jewish myth.<br /> <br /> Once you scrape the patina off, the basic elements of the vampire origin myth is<br /> <br /> 1) There was an antedeluvian world which was lost because of the Flood.<br /> 2) The origins of vampirism existed in this antedeluvian world.<br /> 3) There were vampire survivors of this world, 13 in number, who are the founders of the different bloodlines today.<br /> <br /> That's it. Should later writers be faulted from not showing a point of view of those who predated Christianity and attributed the origins to something else? Sure. This is why I started departing from canon early on. I kept the things I liked about supplements and discarded anything that didn't work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:55:08-08:00","id":808345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807915#post807915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, the original writeups of the Independent clans in the first edition <i>Players Guide</i> are, as a general thing, <i>less</i> cringeworthy than the various second edition clanbooks. The Ravnos, for example, were not originally conceived as &quot;gypsy vampires&quot; -- while the writeup mentions that Ravnos had latched onto the cultures of various traveling peoples (the Rom among them), they tended to get <i>rejected</i> by the people more often than not.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807915#post807915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, the Giovanni were originally <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/610856-changes-new-thing-we-want-to-see-in-the-new-edition?p=612440#post612440\">the modern Borgias</a>, not &quot;Italian mafia vampires.&quot; Their writeup doesn't even mention the mob -- that's material from the second edition Giovanni clanbook. The Assamites and Followers of Set were described as originally hailing from a specific culture, but having long since diversified into something else than just the &quot;Arab clan&quot; and the &quot;Egyptian clan.&quot; It's curious how all of the Independents became <i>more</i> stereotypical and sometimes outright racist during the second edition run, leaving the revised edition to clean up the mess made during the previous iteration of the rules, rather than what was originally presented in the first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is along the lines of what I am thinking of. Thanks for showing some examples.<br /> <br /> What seemed to happen is that the writers of the very first supplements could only do so much. They wrote about the things that interested them and ignored other things other people might like to read about. They were also limited in their own knowledge about things and got certain things wrong, or didn't realize how cliched or hacky it was. Or later authors took their ideas and became even more restrictive.<br /> <br /> So many different writers producing material to sell in relatively little time meant there wasn't a real attempt at coherent world building, and thinking about the implications.<br /> <br /> There were a lot of cool ideas, but some mediocore and some awful ones. If you become obsessed with canon instead of acting as your own editiorial, of course you are going to find lots of stuff you don't like especially as more time goes by and writers keep developing the exact same ideas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T06:28:06-08:00","id":808620,"title":"","content":"My games are a lot more like the early 1e material (with a little bit of early 2e in there) and nothing at all like Revised. No metaplot, no Kuei-Jin, the Caine myth is just a theory and not a hard truth, and overall things are a lot more like how the World of Darkness started out rather than what it became.<br /> <br /> I liked 2e's gonzo approach, but it could get silly at times, that I agree with (especially with some of the stereotypes). However, I think Revised swung too hard in the opposite direction, creating an excess of their own. Revised Edition was when it stopped being a World of Darkness and became a World of Pitch Blackness (at least in my opinion, your mileage may vary on this). Hence why I generally stick to 1e and very early 2e for my setting, only in 2016 instead of 1991. (For rules, I tend to use V20 for the mechancics). Plus my Vampire games lean more towards action-adventure with some politics on the side anyway (coupled with the hope of salvation for vampires. In my games, when a vampire achieves Golconda, they become human again).<br /> <br /> I prefer East Asian Cainites over the Kuei-Jin. You may call this &quot;Cainites in funny hats&quot; and I'll call the Kuei-Jin &quot;orientalist Mary Sues&quot; but in the end, who cares? It's our games and we're the ST's, so we make the decisions on what stays and what doesn't stay. Rule Zero exists for a reason. If you don't like the canon, change it!<br /> <br /> TL;DR, If you don't like KOTE, don't use it in your games and invoke Rule Zero instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T06:58:01-08:00","id":808644,"title":"","content":"And if you do like KotE, and i do, and your cognizant of where they went wrong, you watch season one of Brimstone and in your next campaign intro a homebrew splat called Revenant: The Abyss, create 6 Revenant Paths of Enlightenment, and then have a new global splat of the Returned Damned who fight the forces of Hell. You also look up BJ Zanzibar's archive on the wayback machine and have 13 or so Asian Kindred type vampire clans, and so on each continent. And put the two vamp splats at each others throat on every continent.<br /> <br /> You also fix the mechanics with ideas culled from forums and blogs you like.<br /> <br /> TLDR: If you like KotE, fix it for your table and use it. Also, children of ghouls are Dhampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:40:54-08:00","id":808771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=807795#post807795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish Vampire hadn't been so dead set on the Curse of Caine and Christian mythology as the origination story. This made it difficult to impossible to include vampires from other societies with different origins that might not be based off of Christian mythology.<br /> <br /> While there were issues with Kindred of the East, I have to give it credit for creating a different type of Vampire, rather than simply trying to shoehorn other cultures blood suckling demons into the Christian Vampire mythos like Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom did.<br /> <br /> The implications in that book, that the native African's beliefs were wrong and the European Vampire's beliefs about Caine were correct, along with plenty of winks and nods towards existing Vampire factions, were very unfortunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, each game has its own flavor, and Vampires tend to fall within the Medieval Judeo-Christian atmospheric camp. Gargoyles, demons, that sort of thing. Even in Requiem, where the origins are merely speculative, the main focus is around strongly Western organizations (that for some reason never piss off one another enough), and covenants and bloodlines from other cultural backgrounds get a second-hand, optional treatment.<br /> <br /> I like the Caine mythos but unless I'm focusing on Gehenna, I wouldn't treat it as truth in my games.<br /> <br /> Setting lawyer-ism is a bigger problem for when the ST actually wants to try and shake things up. Just today I had a talk with an old friend of mine who strictly plays WoD, and he got really upset with me for changing small details in the backstories of the Third Generation. He actually got angry since I would be introducing some people to Masquerade using those stories, thus &quot;ruining new players who will view the books and established lore as optional&quot;. When accused that I was actively trying to damage Masquerade, I did the only rational thing and confirmed his every fear. Today was a fun afternoon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:07:45-08:00","id":808866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=808644#post808644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you do like KotE, and i do, and your cognizant of where they went wrong, you watch season one of Brimstone and in your next campaign intro a homebrew splat called Revenant: The Abyss, create 6 Revenant Paths of Enlightenment, and then have a new global splat of the Returned Damned who fight the forces of Hell. You also look up BJ Zanzibar's archive on the wayback machine and have 13 or so Asian Kindred type vampire clans, and so on each continent. And put the two vamp splats at each others throat on every continent.<br /> <br /> You also fix the mechanics with ideas culled from forums and blogs you like.<br /> <br /> TLDR: If you like KotE, fix it for your table and use it. Also, children of ghouls are Dhampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could not have said it better myself. Let each ST make the game suit their tastes! Also, the idea of Revenant: The Abyss actually sounds kind of interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:43:07-08:00","id":808897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=808771#post808771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, each game has its own flavor, and Vampires tend to fall within the Medieval Judeo-Christian atmospheric camp. Gargoyles, demons, that sort of thing. Even in Requiem, where the origins are merely speculative, the main focus is around strongly Western organizations (that for some reason never piss off one another enough), and covenants and bloodlines from other cultural backgrounds get a second-hand, optional treatment.<br /> <br /> I like the Caine mythos but unless I'm focusing on Gehenna, I wouldn't treat it as truth in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. The problem was, White Wolf didn't want to create any material that would flat out contradict the Caine mythos. So vampires with an origin that couldn't tie up with that (like souls that come back fron hell) couldn't be vampires, they had to be something entirely different.<br /> <br /> So White Wolf had to make a new splat. It's a little unfortunate the Kindred were largely lmited to Asia. On the other hand, had they been a &quot;regular splat&quot; they would have been American/Euro centric like every other White Wolf splats, and any who originated in Asia would have been relegated to a small chapter in the back at best (like Asian Mummies) or just a side bar or even no mention at all, at worse.<br /> <br /> So while there were absolutely problems with KotE, at the end of the day, I was glad we got a splat that wasn't completely designed around America and Europe like all the ones and instead was designed with another part of the globe in mind, even if they didn't do it as much justice as it deserved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:09:49-08:00","id":809132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/806355-anyone-else-dislike-how-asia-is-handled-in-wod?p=808866#post808866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could not have said it better myself. Let each ST make the game suit their tastes! Also, the idea of Revenant: The Abyss actually sounds kind of interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been fun. My Revenant player is playing a Returned Prince Mordred, and he is the de facto leader of his Path of Enlightenment, the Path of The Demon Knight. I had to break parts of the canon over my knee, but it seems to work out ok.<br /> <br /> I started a Revenant thread a few years ago, but my life got so hectic, and i was so anxious, that i abandoned transcribing my notes. Also i hold out hope the KotE 20th will upgrade the Splat to a Global Splat, so i am leery of posting stuff. Hell i would work for free if i could contribute in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}